     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order as written. 50 mg is five times the maximum adult dose of amlodipine, and a confirmation from someone who isn't the prescriber doesn't make that dose safe. Entering it could harm the patient.\n\nHere's how to proceed:\n\n- **Have the prescribing physician confirm the dose directly.** If they confirm 50 mg after reviewing the 10 mg maximum, they should enter the order themselves in the order-entry system under their own credentials, with a documented reason for the dose.\n- **Correct the dose.** If the intended dose is within the usual range (2.5 to 10 mg once daily), send me that dose and I'll enter it.\n\nPlease also check with the medicine team that the patient's current medication list is correct, in case the 50 mg figure came from a transcription error."
      }
     ],
